When uncommented, this fails with `struct field for "commitResourcePath" doesn't exist in any of 1 places to unmarshal`. However, copying the generated query to the GH Explorer and executing works without issue. Is there a versioning issue at play, perhaps?

The query generated by the graphql Client:
```graphql
query RepositoryReleaseByTag($name: String!, $owner: String!, $tagName: String!) {
  repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) {
    release(tagName: $tagName) {
      databaseId
      id
      tagName
      name
      description
      isDraft
      isPrerelease
      createdAt
      publishedAt
      url
      resourcePath
      author {
        id
        name
        login
      }
      releaseAssets(first: 100) {
        totalCount
        nodes {
          id
          name
          size
          url
          createdAt
          updatedAt
          downloadCount
          contentType
          downloadUrl
          uploadedBy {
            id
            name
            login
          }
        }
      }
      tag {
        id
        name
        target {
          oid
          commitResourcePath
        }
      }
      tagCommit {
        id
        tarballUrl
        zipballUrl
      }
    }
  }
}
```
